(* ds_schema_lifecycle — an enumeration registry ([STYL.2.15.6]).

   How a fact of a schema leaves working memory, as an integrator sees it:
   retracted by the host, a rule or truth maintenance; retracted at its
   deadline; or owned by the engine. libds's `ds_schema_lifecycle_t` mirrors
   it name for name and value for value. It is not the artefact's scope
   (`proto/schema_logical.proto#SchemaLifecycle`), which answers a different
   question. It travels nowhere, so it is an EBNF registry rather than a
   protobuf ([STYL.5.9.7]).

   The alternation below is the closure: these names and no others.
   Each production is an allocation. A production that is NOT a member
   of the alternation is out of use — the number stays allocated to that
   name ([STYL.2.8.7]). *)

ds_schema_lifecycle = DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_LOGICAL
                    | DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_TTL
                    | DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_INTERNAL ;

(* allocations *)

DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_LOGICAL  = "0" ;
DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_TTL      = "1" ;
DS_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_INTERNAL = "2" ;
